Enhancement: speedup backups/restore on fast connections.

Restic used HTTP/2 connections that multiplex multiple connections to
a host in a single TCP connection. This can severely limit throughput
with very fast connections. Restic now uses multiple HTTP/2
connections by default, one for each connection set in the backend, up
to 128. Backup and restore speeds can increase by ~4.5x on a very fast
connection.

Restore the old behavior with --bypass-http2-multiplexing=false.

